## Problem : Find first and last position of element in sorted array 

## Problem Statement : 

Given an array of integers nums sorted in non-decreasing order, find the starting and ending position of a given target value.

If target is not found in the array, return [-1, -1].

You must write an algorithm with O(log n) runtime complexity.


 ## Example:

Input: nums = [5,7,7,8,8,10], target = 8
Output: [3,4]
Example 2:

Input: nums = [5,7,7,8,8,10], target = 6
Output: [-1,-1]
Example 3:

Input: nums = [], target = 0
Output: [-1,-1]

Input: nums = [0,2,2,2,2,2,7,7,10] , target = 2
output : [1,5]

## Approach :
Binary Search Algorithm 
- Find a first occurance using binary search algorithm and if target is found so save the index in the answer variable  then we have to move the right pointer with mid - 1 and find again 
most first occurance, when left is greater than right we have to stop here 
- same logic will use for a last occurance and where we move left pointer with mid + 1
- return answer from both function and return the answer in the array.

## Code :

class Solution {
    public int[] searchRange(int[] nums, int target) {

        int left = firstOccurance(nums,target);
       int right =  lastOccurance(nums,target);
          return new int[]{left,right};
    }

        private static int firstOccurance(int nums[],int target){

        
        int left = 0;
        int right = nums.length - 1;
        int mid = 0;
        int ans = -1;
        while(left <= right){
            mid = left + (right - left) / 2;
            if(nums[mid] == target){
                ans = mid;
                right = mid - 1;
  }
            else if(nums[mid] < target){
                left = mid + 1;
            }
            else {
                right = mid - 1;
            }
        }

        return ans;
        
    }


        private static int lastOccurance(int nums[],int target){

        
        int left = 0;
        int right = nums.length - 1;
        int mid = 0;
        int ans = -1;
        while(left <= right){
            mid = left + (right - left) / 2;
            if(nums[mid] == target){
                ans = mid;
                left = mid + 1;
  }
            else if(nums[mid] < target){
                left = mid + 1;
            }
            else {
                right = mid - 1;
            }
        }

        return ans;
        
    }
}

## Complexity : TC ; O(log n)
Sc : O(1)

O(log n) + O(log n)
= O(2 log n)
= O(log n)
